  (text "Bias network R502/Q501/R504/R505/Q502/R503 draws about 2 mA of quiescent current.\n(24 V - 2 diode drops = 22.8 V.  22.8 V/11260 Ω = 2.0 mA)\n\nBase of Q503 in the quiescent state will be roughy 0.66 volts, 0.06 volts above a diode drop.\nEmitter of Q503 will therefore be about 0.06 V,\nso R506 will be drawing a little over 10 mA.\n\nSame argument applies to the base of Q504.  Both transistors will therefore\nbe in their active regions and passing a small amount of current when\nin the crossover region.\n\n100 Ω resistor between the op amp output and the circuit output is no longer needed.\n\n100 mA is a safe current as long as the load is at least 55 ohms. The op-amp clips at\nabout ±10 V, and a 60 ohm load (R506 + R508) will drop 6 volts.  4 volts and 100 mA is\nwell within Q503's safe operating area.\n\nLighter loads will require a larger R506 (dissipating power!) a restricted input voltage,\nor both.\n\n\n"
    (at 161.29 87.63 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 5a25c0ed-d262-4413-b554-c8f470bace54)
  )

